1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,200
Breaking software into parts is easy. Breaking the customer's problem into useful outcomes is different.

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:12,733
A database, an API, a screen: these organize an answer we've already imagined.

3
00:00:12,733 --> 00:00:16,300
But development also means discovering which answer works.

4
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:19,167
Say shoppers want to avoid wasted trips.

5
00:00:19,167 --> 00:00:23,267
First, let them check whether one item is in stock at one store.

6
00:00:23,267 --> 00:00:25,767
Opening hours and reservations can wait.

7
00:00:25,767 --> 00:00:28,200
Two premises guide this approach.

8
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:32,100
Look for smaller customer problems before deciding the solution.

9
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:35,700
And treat the plan as an attempt, never a guarantee.

10
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:37,867
Then optimize for two things.

11
00:00:37,867 --> 00:00:42,200
First: each completed story delivers useful value people can evaluate.

12
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:45,167
Show the stock result. Ask what happened.

13
00:00:45,167 --> 00:00:47,833
Build just enough, just in time to learn.

14
00:00:47,833 --> 00:00:50,633
Second: keep the freedom to change direction.

15
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:54,367
If feedback makes opening hours more important, choose that next.

16
00:00:54,367 --> 00:00:58,367
Keep the useful stock check. Leave reservations unstarted.

17
00:00:58,367 --> 00:01:02,667
At completed boundaries, avoid unfinished waste and damage to the product.

18
00:01:02,667 --> 00:01:04,733
Four principles make this work.

19
00:01:04,733 --> 00:01:11,700
Valuable, visible, vertical: a useful result, recognizable to users, working through every required part.

20
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:15,200
One-piece flow: finish one customer outcome together.

21
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:19,000
Repeat at smaller scales. Every commit is your last commit.

22
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:24,133
Strive for value now; serve today's purpose or an existing documented need, including product health.

23
00:01:24,133 --> 00:01:26,367
And care for the whole product.

24
00:01:26,367 --> 00:01:30,467
Change whichever parts the outcome requires; leave a coherent design.

25
00:01:30,467 --> 00:01:37,100
That preserves option value: speculative future possibilities at a given cost, without building unused features now.

26
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:42,900
Smaller problems. Useful answers. Freedom to choose again.
